WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.320
Views of the police dropped sharply after the&nbsp;
murder of George Floyd. But in several new polls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.520
they have rebounded somewhat. In a Harris/Harvard&nbsp;
Center for American Political Studies poll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.920
69 percent said they had a favorable view of the&nbsp;
police, up from 60 percent a year ago. Gallup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:28.320
reported recently that confidence in the police among whites&nbsp;
was virtually identical to what it was in June 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:34.320
but that black confidence had ticked up from an&nbsp;
abysmal 19 percent to 27 percent.&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.040
Black and white views of the police have&nbsp;
differed for a long time, but in recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.160
white views about unfair treatment of blacks&nbsp;
by the police have moved closer to black ones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.000
Neither group wants to defund the&nbsp;
police. In a June 2021 USA Today/Ipsos poll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.400
just 22 percent said they supported&nbsp;
the movement to defund the police.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.240
Sixteen percent of whites and 38&nbsp;
percent of blacks wanted to defund.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.200
Eighty percent of whites and 64 percent of blacks&nbsp;
wanted to deploy more police to the streets.&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.320
How confident are you about the police in&nbsp;
your community? Let us know in our poll. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.240
let us know what other topics you'd like&nbsp;
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.560
and be sure to like and subscribe for&nbsp;
more research and videos from AEI.

